  "alphabetical-order-sorter/content/explainer.md": "# How Alphabetical Order Sorter Works\n\nThe Alphabetical Order Sorter organizes lists of words, names, citations, and numbers into ordered sequences using international Unicode Collation via `Intl.Collator`.\n\n## Natural Number Sorting vs Binary Sorting\nStandard binary ASCII sorting compares character codepoints sequentially. In standard ASCII ordering, `\"10\"` sorts before `\"2\"` because the character `'1'` precedes `'2'`. When **Natural Numbers** is enabled, numeric sequences inside text strings are parsed as discrete numerical magnitudes, ordering `2` before `10` naturally as humans expect.\n\n## International Collation & Case Sensitivity\nThe sorter relies on the native ECMAScript Internationalization API (`Intl.Collator`). Rather than performing simple uppercase transformations that break accented characters (like `é` or `ü`), the collator applies standard linguistic rules. Case-insensitive mode treats letters with identical base glyphs as equivalent while preserving original capitalization.\n\n## Stable Sorting & Deduplication\n- **Algorithm Stability:** JavaScript's sorting implementation preserves the original relative position of items that evaluate to equal comparison values.\n- **Duplicate Removal:** When deduplication is active, the engine tracks seen keys in a set. It retains the very first occurrence of an item and discards subsequent duplicates, reporting both total item count and removed duplicate counts live.\n- **Sort by Last Word:** Extracts the final token of each line to alphabetize lists of people's full names by surname effortlessly.\n\n## Delimiter Handling and Academic Indexing\nWriters, legal researchers, and academics often manage bibliographies and indexes separated by different delimiters. The tool permits toggling dynamically between line breaks, comma-separated lists, and tab-separated entries. Automatic whitespace trimming strips accidental leading spaces so punctuation and indentations do not misplace alphabetized entries. Everything processes in real-time in your browser without data transmission.",
  "alphabetical-order-sorter/content/faqs.json": "{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"how-does-natural-numeric-sorting-work\",\n      \"question\": \"What is natural numeric sorting?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Standard alphabetical sorting places \\\"10\\\" before \\\"2\\\". Natural sorting treats embedded numbers as quantities so that 2 comes before 10.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"stable-sorting-guarantee\",\n      \"question\": \"Is the sorting algorithm stable?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes. When items compare equal (for instance, case-insensitive duplicates like \\\"Apple\\\" and \\\"apple\\\"), their original relative order is strictly preserved.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"how-does-duplicate-removal-work\",\n      \"question\": \"How does duplicate removal handle letter casing?\",\n      \"answer\": \"When duplicate removal is enabled with case-insensitivity, the tool keeps the very first occurrence found in the list and removes subsequent variants.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"sorting-by-last-name-or-word\",\n      \"question\": \"Can I sort a list of full names by last name?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes. Enabling \\\"Sort by Last Word\\\" extracts the trailing word of each entry (such as the surname) to collate names alphabetically.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"delimiters-supported\",\n      \"question\": \"What input delimiters can I use?\",\n      \"answer\": \"You can split items by line breaks, commas, semicolons, whitespace, tabs, or a custom delimiter string.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"unicode-character-collation\",\n      \"question\": \"Does the sorter handle accented letters and non-English alphabets?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes. Collation is powered by Intl.Collator which respects international language collation rules, correctly grouping accented and non-Latin characters.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"idempotency-guarantee\",\n      \"question\": \"Is sorting idempotent?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes. Sorting an already sorted list produces the identical list without alterations, verified by automated fast-check property testing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"sorting-direction-options\",\n      \"question\": \"Can I reverse the sort order?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes. You can switch between Ascending (A to Z, lowest to highest) and Descending (Z to A, highest to lowest) with a single click.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
  "alphabetical-order-sorter/content/privacy.md": "## Privacy Policy for {{siteName}}\n\n**Effective Date:** {{effectiveDate}}\n\nAt {{siteName}} (available at {{domain}}), we take your privacy seriously. This Privacy Policy describes how we handle information when you visit or use {{toolName}}.\n\n## 1. Client-Side Only Processing\n\nAll computations, conversions, and data processing in {{toolName}} happen entirely within your web browser. \n\n- **No User Data Transmission:** Your inputs, values, files, or calculations are never sent to our servers or any third-party servers.\n- **No Remote Storage:** We do not collect, log, store, or transmit any data you enter into the tool.\n- **Data Retention:** Once you close or refresh your browser tab, all entered inputs and generated results are cleared from browser memory.\n\n## 2. Cookies and Local Storage\n\nThe site itself does not set or use tracking cookies.\n\n{{#if localStorage}}\n### Local Storage\nWe use browser local storage solely to remember non-identifying user interface preferences between visits. Specifically, we store the following keys:\n- `{{localStorageKeys}}`\n\nThis data remains stored locally on your device and is never transmitted to us. You can clear local storage at any time via your browser settings.\n{{/if}}\n\n{{#if ads}}\n### Advertising\nWe may display third-party advertisements to support the operation of this free utility. These advertising partners may use cookies, web beacons, or similar tracking technologies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website or other sites on the Internet. You can manage your ad personalization settings or opt out of interest-based advertising by visiting [About Ads](https://www.aboutads.info/choices/) or [Network Advertising Initiative](https://www.networkadvertising.org/choices/).\n{{/if}}\n\n{{#if analytics}}\n### Analytics\nWe use privacy-respecting analytics to collect aggregated, anonymous traffic metrics (such as page views, referrer sources, and browser types) to understand how visitors use the site. No personal identifiers or calculation inputs are ever tracked or tied to your browsing session.\n{{/if}}\n\n## 3. Server Logging\n\nLike virtually all web hosts, the infrastructure hosting {{domain}} may record standard technical server logs. These logs may include your IP address, browser user-agent, requested URL, and access timestamps. These logs are maintained by our hosting provider for infrastructure security, DDoS mitigation, and operational integrity, and are not combined with any calculation data.\n\n## 4. Changes to This Policy\n\nWe may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated effective date.\n\n## 5. Contact Us\n\nIf you have questions or concerns regarding this Privacy Policy, please contact us at:\n- **Email:** {{contactEmail}}\n- **Website:** {{domain}}\n\n",
