  "background-image/content/explainer.md": "# How Background Image Maker Works\n\nThe Background Image Maker synthesizes crisp, custom background graphics, desktop wallpapers, and social media backdrops entirely within your browser using the HTML5 Canvas API.\n\n## Algorithmic Generation Modes\nInstead of downloading heavy static stock imagery across a network, this utility renders procedural visuals locally on your hardware:\n- **Linear & Radial Gradients:** Color transitions are interpolated mathematically across directional vector angles using Canvas 2D linear gradient contexts. Every color stop and angular offset is mapped directly to standard CSS syntax for immediate export to web stylesheets.\n- **Geometric Texture Patterns:** Crisp vector-style polka dots, structural wireframe grids, and diagonal hatch stripes are drawn with customizable pixel steps and transparency values.\n- **Photo Backdrops with Gaussian Blur:** If you choose to supply your own local photo, it is loaded directly into browser memory using `createImageBitmap`. You can apply adjustable Gaussian blur radii and semi-transparent dark or colored scrims to create high-contrast backdrop images ideal for text overlay.\n\n## Technical Specifications & Canvas Boundaries\nThe engine accommodates standard display presets—such as Full HD (1920×1080), 2K QHD (2560×1440), 4K UHD (3840×2160), and phone portrait aspect ratios (1080×1920)—while permitting custom dimensions up to 8192 pixels per side. Hardware-accelerated GPU blitting ensures that rendering 4K buffers takes under 100 milliseconds without UI lag.\n\n## Dual Output: CSS Stylesheets and Bitmap Downloads\nDesigners can toggle between copying clean CSS gradient code blocks directly into their stylesheets and downloading high-resolution PNG or JPEG image assets. Because the color stops map cleanly to W3C CSS specifications, web developers can test visual layouts in the live canvas before committing identical color tokens to their CSS or Tailwind design system.\n\n## Privacy & Security\nZero external network calls are made. No telemetry, analytics, or image bytes ever leave your local machine, guaranteeing complete confidentiality for personal photographs and proprietary brand palettes.",
  "background-image/content/faqs.json": "{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"how-are-backgrounds-generated\",\n      \"question\": \"How are backgrounds generated without a server or stock photos?\",\n      \"answer\": \"All graphics, mathematical gradients, and geometric patterns are synthesized on an HTML5 Canvas directly in your web browser. Nothing is fetched from or sent to a remote server.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"supported-resolutions\",\n      \"question\": \"What image resolutions and aspect ratios can I export?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Standard presets include Full HD (1920x1080), 2K QHD (2560x1440), 4K UHD (3840x2160), Mobile Portrait (1080x1920), and 720p HD. You can also define custom canvas dimensions up to 8192 pixels.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"css-gradient-code\",\n      \"question\": \"Can I copy the CSS code for web design?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes. Whenever you design a linear or radial gradient, the exact CSS rule is generated with angle and color stops ready to copy into your stylesheet.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"image-overlay-blur-privacy\",\n      \"question\": \"Is my uploaded photo kept private when creating a blurred wallpaper?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Completely private. When you upload a picture, it is loaded into your browser memory via createImageBitmap. No bytes ever leave your device.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"file-formats-available\",\n      \"question\": \"Which file formats can I download?\",\n      \"answer\": \"You can export high-quality PNG for lossless graphics, JPEG with clean background rendering, or modern WebP.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"conic-and-radial-gradients\",\n      \"question\": \"How do radial gradients adapt to widescreen displays?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Radial gradients compute center coordinates and maximum ellipse radiuses dynamically based on your chosen canvas aspect ratio to ensure uniform color spreading.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"pattern-density-scaling\",\n      \"question\": \"How does geometric pattern scaling work?\",\n      \"answer\": \"You can adjust grid, dot, or stripe step sizes from 10 to 100 pixels with adjustable opacity overlays, enabling subtle textural depth without overwhelming UI elements.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"performance-on-4k-displays\",\n      \"question\": \"Will generating 4K wallpapers slow down my computer?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Canvas operations utilize hardware-accelerated rendering through your graphics card, making 4K rasterization nearly instantaneous while consuming minimal memory.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
