  "image-to-pdf/content/explainer.md": "# How Image to PDF Converter Works\n\nThe Image to PDF Converter compiles individual image files into a single, multipage PDF document using the pure JavaScript library `pdf-lib` executing directly in the client browser.\n\n## Typographic Geometry & Placement\nPDF coordinates are defined in typographic points, where 1 inch equals exactly 72 points:\n- **A4 Standard:** 595.28 × 841.89 pt (210 × 297 mm)\n- **US Letter:** 612.00 × 792.00 pt (8.5 × 11.0 in)\n- **Fit to Image:** Creates a custom page bounding box matching the image pixel dimensions plus specified margin padding.\n\nWhen calculating layout in **Contain** mode, available printable width and height are determined by subtracting twice the margin parameter:\n```text\navailWidth = pageWidth - (2 * margin)\navailHeight = pageHeight - (2 * margin)\nscale = Math.min(availWidth / imageWidth, availHeight / imageHeight)\n```\nThe image is drawn at `x = margin + (availWidth - drawnWidth) / 2` and `y = margin + (availHeight - drawnHeight) / 2`, centering the photograph on the page without distorting its natural aspect ratio.\n\n## Binary Embedding\nJPEG and PNG image streams are embedded into the PDF document as discrete XObject image dictionaries. Non-standard or raw graphic buffers are first normalized into standard PNG streams using HTML5 Canvas before document inclusion.\n\n## Document Customization and Print Readiness\nUsers can arrange input images into sequential pages, set landscape or portrait orientations per document, and adjust margin spacing to suit physical binder borders (18 pt for compact margins or 36 pt for standard half-inch print margins). Because image streams retain their intrinsic color profiles without re-sampling, generated PDFs maintain high-resolution sharpness suitable for formal government applications, academic course submissions, and professional printing.\n\n## Local Execution\nAll document assembly occurs within browser WebAssembly and JavaScript threads. No documents, invoices, or ID scans are ever uploaded to a cloud server, ensuring full regulatory compliance and personal privacy.",
  "image-to-pdf/content/faqs.json": "{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"how-are-images-compiled-into-pdf\",\n      \"question\": \"How are images converted into PDF without a backend?\",\n      \"answer\": \"This tool uses the pdf-lib library running natively in your browser. Each uploaded image is scaled and embedded onto document pages according to your layout preferences.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"supported-page-sizes\",\n      \"question\": \"What page sizes and orientations can I choose?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Standard A4 (595.28 x 841.89 pt), US Letter (612 x 792 pt), and Fit-to-Image modes are supported in Portrait, Landscape, or Auto orientation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"can-i-reorder-images\",\n      \"question\": \"Can I change the order of pages before downloading?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes. You can use the Move Up and Move Down controls on each image to arrange pages exactly as desired.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"margin-and-fit-options\",\n      \"question\": \"What margin and image scaling options are available?\",\n      \"answer\": \"You can choose between zero margin, 18 pt (small), or 36 pt (standard), with options to Contain (preserve aspect ratio), Cover, or Stretch images across the page.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"is-my-document-private\",\n      \"question\": \"Is my document private and secure?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Completely private. No image bytes or generated PDF documents ever leave your device or travel over the network.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"aspect-ratio-preservation\",\n      \"question\": \"Will my photos be stretched or distorted in the PDF?\",\n      \"answer\": \"In the default Contain mode, the engine calculates uniform proportional scaling so images are centered without any aspect ratio distortion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"pdf-standard-compliance\",\n      \"question\": \"Are the created PDF documents compatible with all PDF readers?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes. Generated documents conform strictly to the PDF 1.7 specification, rendering consistently across Adobe Acrobat, Apple Preview, Google Chrome, and mobile viewers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"maximum-pages-allowed\",\n      \"question\": \"Is there a limit on how many images can be compiled into one PDF?\",\n      \"answer\": \"You can compile dozens of images simultaneously. Memory management ensures buffers are processed sequentially into the PDF binary structure.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
