  "jpg-to-png/content/explainer.md": "# How JPG to PNG Converter Works\n\nThe JPG to PNG Converter decodes JPEG raster images locally and re-encodes them into the lossless Portable Network Graphics (PNG) format using the HTML5 Canvas API.\n\n## Technical Realities of Format Conversion\nUnderstanding the differences between lossy and lossless image codecs is crucial when converting files:\n1. **The Irreversibility of JPEG Loss:** When an image is saved as a JPEG, a discrete cosine transform discards high-frequency visual information to minimize file size. Converting that file into a PNG cannot reconstruct the discarded frequencies; it simply captures the currently visible pixels into a lossless wrapper.\n2. **File Size Expansion:** JPEG compression achieves ratios of 10:1 to 20:1. Because PNG preserves the exact RGB value of every decoded pixel using DEFLATE compression, the resulting PNG is typically 2 to 5 times larger than the input JPEG.\n3. **Prevention of Further Degradation:** The primary benefit of converting to PNG is preventing *generation loss*. Editing and re-saving an image as JPEG compounds compression artifacts, whereas editing a PNG preserves quality across successive saves.\n\n## Browser-Side Conversion Flow\nWhen a user selects files, each image is loaded into memory via an `HTMLImageElement` object. An off-screen canvas is dimensioned to the image's intrinsic width and height. The pixel buffer is transferred to the canvas and serialized to an `image/png` blob. Multiple files can be packed into a ZIP archive in memory using `fflate` without server round-trips.\n\n## Transparency and Graphic Design Preparation\nWhile source JPEGs do not support transparent backgrounds, converting them to PNG establishes an RGBA pixel buffer with a 32-bit alpha channel. This format serves as the foundational starting point for graphic designers and digital artists preparing product photos, icons, and logo assets for background extraction, layer compositing, and vector masking in photo editing software. Zero bytes are uploaded to remote servers, safeguarding sensitive commercial imagery.",
  "jpg-to-png/content/faqs.json": "{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"does-converting-jpg-to-png-improve-quality\",\n      \"question\": \"Does converting JPG to PNG improve image quality?\",\n      \"answer\": \"No. While PNG is a lossless format, converting an existing JPG cannot restore compression artifacts or visual details that JPEG lossy compression already discarded.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"why-are-png-files-larger\",\n      \"question\": \"Why are converted PNG files often larger than the original JPG?\",\n      \"answer\": \"PNG uses lossless DEFLATE compression which preserves exact pixel color values, whereas JPEG uses lossy discrete cosine transform. Consequently, converted PNG files are almost always larger.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"batch-conversion-and-zip\",\n      \"question\": \"Can I convert multiple JPGs and download them as a ZIP archive?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes. You can select multiple images to convert them in batch, downloading them individually or bundled together in a ZIP file.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"privacy-guarantee\",\n      \"question\": \"Are my images uploaded to any remote server?\",\n      \"answer\": \"No. The conversion is performed locally via your browser HTML5 Canvas. No image data is ever uploaded or transmitted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"supported-input-formats\",\n      \"question\": \"Can I convert other formats to PNG?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes. The converter accepts JPG, JPEG, WebP, and BMP files and converts them all into standard lossless PNG.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"lossless-compression-algorithm\",\n      \"question\": \"How does the PNG format compress image data?\",\n      \"answer\": \"PNG uses LZ77-derived DEFLATE compression paired with predictive horizontal/vertical byte filters to pack repeated color runs without discarding data.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"transparency-support\",\n      \"question\": \"Does converting JPG to PNG add a transparent background?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Converting JPG creates an opaque PNG since JPEGs contain no alpha channel. To add transparency, pixels must be edited or keyed out separately.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"when-to-use-png-over-jpg\",\n      \"question\": \"When is PNG preferred over JPG for graphics?\",\n      \"answer\": \"PNG is ideal for digital illustrations, screenshots, UI diagrams, and typography where sharp edge definitions and color consistency are essential.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
