  "wifi-qr-code-generator/content/explainer.md": "# How Wi-Fi QR Code Generator Works\n\nThe Wi-Fi QR Code Generator translates wireless network credentials into standardized barcode payloads recognized by iOS, Android, and modern camera scanners.\n\n## The ZXing Wi-Fi Payload Standard\nThe generated QR code contains a structured payload formatted according to the ZXing protocol:\n```text\nWIFI:T:<WPA|WEP|nopass>;S:<ssid>;P:<password>;H:<true|false>;;\n```\n- **Authentication (`T`):** Represents the encryption standard (`WPA` for WPA/WPA2/WPA3, `WEP`, or `nopass`).\n- **Network Name (`S`):** The Service Set Identifier (SSID).\n- **Password (`P`):** The network pre-shared key.\n- **Hidden Network (`H`):** Included only when the network does not broadcast its beacon.\n\n## Delimiter Escaping Rules\nBecause semicolons (`;`), colons (`:`), and backslashes (`\\`) serve as protocol delimiters, any occurrence of these characters inside the SSID or password is escaped with a backslash. For example, an SSID named `Home;Net` and password `p:ss\\word` are serialized as `S:Home\\;Net;P:p\\:ss\\\\word;;`. Additionally, strings containing purely hexadecimal characters are wrapped in quotation marks to prevent misinterpretation as raw WEP keys.\n\n## Vector SVG and High-Resolution Printing\nUsers can download generated barcodes as crisp scalable vector graphics (SVG) or high-resolution PNG bitmaps. Because SVG files scale infinitely without pixelation, graphic designers can embed codes directly into signage, acrylic desk plaques, and tabletop stand cards for coffee shops, offices, and guest suites. The tool also provides a one-click print card button with clean CSS media rules tailored for standard desktop printers.\n\n## Client-Side Security & Plaintext Caveat\nThe QR code is generated 100% locally in your browser using client-side JavaScript. No network parameters are sent across the internet. However, because QR codes are an unencrypted visual representation, anyone with physical access to scan the code can extract the plain text password. For sensitive environments, place printed cards in controlled guest reception areas.",
  "wifi-qr-code-generator/content/faqs.json": "{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"how-do-wifi-qr-codes-work\",\n      \"question\": \"How do Wi-Fi QR codes connect devices automatically?\",\n      \"answer\": \"The QR code encodes a standard ZXing Wi-Fi configuration payload (WIFI:T:...;S:...;P:...;;). When scanned with iOS Camera or Android, the device automatically parses the SSID and credentials to connect.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"is-my-password-stored-or-transmitted\",\n      \"question\": \"Is my network password saved or sent over the internet?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Never. The QR code is generated 100% locally in your web browser. Note, however, that anyone who physically scans the code can view your network password in plain text.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"escaping-special-characters\",\n      \"question\": \"How are special characters in SSIDs and passwords handled?\",\n      \"answer\": \"In accordance with the ZXing Wi-Fi QR specification, characters including colons, semicolons, commas, and backslashes are escaped with a preceding backslash.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"print-friendly-wifi-cards\",\n      \"question\": \"Can I print a guest Wi-Fi card to display?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes. Use the \\\"Print Guest Card\\\" button to trigger a clean printable layout formatted specifically for tabletop or wall display.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"hidden-networks-support\",\n      \"question\": \"Does this work for hidden Wi-Fi networks?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes. Enabling the \\\"Hidden Network\\\" checkbox appends H:true to the configuration payload so devices scan for non-broadcasting SSIDs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"wpa3-and-wpa2-compatibility\",\n      \"question\": \"Are modern WPA3 networks supported?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes. Modern mobile operating systems recognize the standard T:WPA token for all WPA, WPA2, and WPA3 Personal networks.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"open-unencrypted-networks\",\n      \"question\": \"Can I generate a QR code for open networks without a password?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes. Selecting the \\\"None / Open\\\" security option omits the password field and sets T:nopass, allowing guests to join open Wi-Fi with one tap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"vector-svg-vs-png-export\",\n      \"question\": \"What is the advantage of downloading SVG over PNG?\",\n      \"answer\": \"SVG is an infinitely scalable vector format that ensures sharp, pixel-perfect printing on posters and signage at any physical print size.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
